    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 11</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.1"/> hwa þonne þegna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.2"/> sig, þe on his boclande cyrican<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.3"/> hæbbe, þe legerstow on sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.4"/>, gesylle þone þriddan dæl his agenre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.5"/> teoþunge into his cyrican.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa þonne þegen sy, þe on his boclande cyricean habbe, þe legerstow on sy, gesylle þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.1-4"/> þriddan dæl his ágene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.1-4"/> teoþunge into his cyrican.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis tainus in hereditate sua terram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.star"/> habeat, in qua cimiterium sit, det ibi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.1-2"/> tertiam partem proprię<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.2-2"/> decimę suę.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.1-3"/><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Si liberalis homo, quem Angli<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.2-3"/> þegen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.3-2"/> uocant, habet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.4-2"/> in alodio (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.5-2"/> est bocland) suo ęcclesiam, quę habeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.6"/> cimiterium, tertiam partem decimę proprię<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_11.lnote.oe.7"/> terrę suę det illi ęcclesię.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis autem uirronum in sua libera terra ecclesiam habeat, tertiam partem proprie decime det sue ecclesie.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="11" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="164" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf hwa þonne þegna<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#ICn_11.robnote.fn.6"/> sig þe on his boclande cyrican hæbbe þe legerstow on sig, gesylle þone<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#ICn_11.robnote.fn.7"/> þriddan dæl his agenre teoþunge into his cyrican.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="244" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gyf hwa þonne þegna sig þe on his boclande cyrican hæbbe, þe legerstow on sig, gesylle þone þriddan dæl his agenre teoþunge into his cyrican.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn [es] aber einer der Adligen ist, der auf seinem kraft Urkunden[privilegs besessenen] Lande<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_11.lnote.de.1"/> eine Kirche hat, an der ein Friedhof liegt, so zahle er ein Drittel des auf ihm [lastenden] Zehnten an diese seine Kirche.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If, however, it is one of the thegns who has on his bookland a church at which there is a graveyard, let him pay a third of the tithe [owed] by him to [this] his church.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_11.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="165" ed="#robertson"/>If, however, there is any thegn who, on the land which he holds by title deed<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_11.robnote.n.2"/>, has a church to which a graveyard is attached, he shall give the third part of his own tithes to his church.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="245" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Yet if there is a thane who has a church possessing a graveyard on land he holds by charter, he is to give one-third of his own tithes to his church.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="295"><ref target="clause:IIEg_2">II Eg 2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II Eg. 2</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_2">II Eg 2–2.2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 11-11:2: II Eg 2-2:2</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="25"><label>derives from</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_2">II Eg 2</ref> <quote>Previous Cnut clauses on 'old minster' entitlements, largely derived from laws of Edgar</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="38"><label>word for word</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_2">II Eg 2–2.1</ref> <quote>If then there be any thegn [word for word as 3.] the nine parts.</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Quadr. writes ‘terram’ but means ‘ecclesiam’. Liebermann compares II Eg 2.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 295, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þegen sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þegen sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cean <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cean Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy, geselle þoñe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy, geselle þoñe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Quadr. meint</hi> ecclesiam</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Quadr. means ecclesiam</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt KR</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in KR</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hinter</hi> I 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">after I 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">the. <hi rend="italic">H</hi>; thein <hi rend="italic">S</hi>; u. þ. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the. H; thein S; u. þ. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">habeat <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">habeat Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. b. <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. H</hi>; <hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. b. written above H; missing in Cb Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">habet <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">habet Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. t. <hi rend="italic">später am Rande Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. t. later in the margin Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_11.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu den 3 Übersetzungen, die nur je eine Seite des zu ihrer Zeit nicht mehr lebendigen Institutes <hi rend="italic">bocland</hi> treffen, <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the 3 translations, each of which captures only one aspect of the institution of <hi rend="italic">bocland</hi>, no longer a living one in their time, <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1a</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_11.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the two following, cf. II Edg. 2 ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_11.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Translated <hi rend="italic">in hereditate sua</hi>, Q; <hi rend="italic">in alodio suo</hi>, Inst.; <hi rend="italic">in sua libera terra</hi>, Cons.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_11.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><label>þegna</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þegen</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_11.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><label>þone</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þonne</hi> A.</seg></note>
      </div>
